New exact constraints:
  stationarity marginals:
    For each substring pattern, the maximum selected-support count over all
    positions in a window is bounded by its common cyclic multiplicity
    marginal. Widths 1 through 7 are active for n=9 when the equivalent
    width-8 repeat-defect inequality is already enabled.
  Walsh aggregates:
    Radius-1 covering rows imply paired Walsh-transform inequalities for every
    nonzero Hamming-ball eigenvalue. These dense aggregate rows are tested but
    remain disabled by default.
  autocorrelation:
    Shift distances are even.
    Radius-1 coverage bounds both differences and agreements for every shift.
    Exact odd shift-orbits force at least one agreement per orbit.

Scope of the strengthening:
  Stationarity, Walsh, and autocorrelation parity are propagation consequences
  of constraints already required by a valid cyclic cover.
  The radius-1 autocorrelation rows are valid weakened cover aggregates.
  The odd-orbit upper bound is necessary for one connected cyclic sequence.
  None of these constraints is by itself a new lower-bound theorem.

Validation:
  focused OR-Tools tests: 28 passed
  stationarity identity: exhaustively checked on small cycles
  Walsh inequality: exhaustively checked on small covering supports
  autocorrelation identities and bounds: exhaustively checked on small cycles
  model coefficients: checked directly in the CP-SAT model proto
  valid Walsh order filtering: checked
  exact and at-most applicability: checked
  separate mathematical and code reviews: no correctness blocker found

