Anchor-256 scope:
  In the disjoint partition, anchor 256 forces every earlier word in
  B_1(0^9) absent. Edge 256 enters vertex zero, while both outgoing edges 0
  and 1 are absent, contradicting balance. This excludes only that partitioned
  anchor case.

Conclusion:
  No length-70 sequence with support size 69 was found.
  No global support-size-69 impossibility proof was produced.
  All ten scheduled bounded anchor runs were executed.
  Each UNKNOWN status is a timeout, not evidence of unsatisfiability.
  Support sizes 68 through 62 at length 70 remain unsearched by this portfolio.
  A lower bound of 71 would additionally require every admissible length from
  62 through 69, unless a separate monotonicity theorem is proved.
  The public mathematical interval remains 62 <= L(9,1) <= 71.
